G2819.definition:
κλῆρος , -ου, ὁ 
 [in LXX chiefly for נַחֲלָה גּוֹרָל ;] 
 a lot ; 
 __(a)  that which is cast or drawn :  Mat.27:35 ,  Mrk.15:24 ,  Luk.23:34 ,  Jhn.19:24 " (LXX),  Act.1:26;  
 __(b)  that which is obtained by casting :  Act.1:17 8:21 ; of a part in the Kingdom of God (cf. Wis 55),  Act.26:18 ,  Col.1:12 ; pl. of the "cure" of a presbyter,  1Pe.5:3  (see  ICC , in l).†
 (AS)

G2822.definition:
κλητός , -ή, -όν
 (καλέω), [in LXX for קָרָא, מִקְרָא,  Exo.12:16 , al. ;] 
called, invited (as to a banquet, Æsch.,  1Sa 1:41 ,  3Ma.5:14 ); in NT, always of the Divine call; 
 __(a)  to some office : κ. ἀπόστολος,  Rom.1:1 ,  1Co.1:1 ; 
 __(b)  to salvation :  Rom.8:28 ,  1Co.1:24 ,  Ju 1 ; κ. καὶ ἐκλεκτοὶ κ. πιστοί,  Rev.17:14;  in gosp. (not in pl., see: καλέω) disting. fr.ἐκλεκτός,  Mat.20:16  (WH, txt., R, omit),  Mat.22:14;  κ. Ἰησοῦ Χρ.,  Rom.1:6;  κ. ἅγιοι, saints by calling,  Rom.1:7 ,  1Co.1:2 .†
 (AS)
